ls to enter the lagoon.","conflict":"The lock oath demands clearing before the spring tide, but the guild still holds the calendar and Pell arrives to see the failure himself.","outcome":"Pell sees the sills for himself and cannot deny what his own tide tables said, while Mara and Sana's evidence is now visible to all.","depends_on":["scn_guild_hall_failure"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spring Tide","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_speaks","title":"Mara Carries the Proof","summary":"Mara returns to the guild hall with Sana, terrace families and the sounding poles, and lets witnesses speak beside her, claiming her mother's name rather than fearing it.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Convince the guild to halt the firing season and release hands for dredging.","conflict":"Pell, unable to admit his earlier trade-off, resists while his guild's families fear lost wages.","outcome":"Pell concedes the season must pause, choosing the lagoon over the calendar, and offers the guild's hands.","depends_on":["scn_silted_sill"]},{"id":"scn_dredge_the_gates","title":"Dredging the Gates","summary":"Guild artisans, terrace families, wardens and Sana's barge dredge the gate channels through the night as the spring tide approaches, Mara reading the settle lines as the work proceeds.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Clear the sills before the spring tide arrives.","conflict":"Time is short, and Pell and Sana must work side by side while Mara must trust others to hold the gate rather than carrying everything herself.","outcome":"The gates are cleared just as the spring tide arrives, and the flood enters the lagoon and restores the tide-mills.","depends_on":["scn_mara_speaks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Tide Returns","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_to_terraces","title":"Silt to the Terraces","summary":"Sana's barge hauls the fertile silt to the Mangrove Terraces, where families spread it as the silt-debt rule demands, and Sana's cooperative earns the dredging contract with its rights recognised.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_sana_duro","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Honour the silt-debt rule and settle the cooperative's contract.","conflict":"Cooperative and terrace families still disagree about shares, and Sana must listen rather than bargain.","outcome":"A fair arrangement is reached on silt shares, and the cooperative's contract is secured.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_the_gates"]},{"id":"scn_new_calendar","title":"A New Calendar","summary":"Pell publicly amends the firing calendar to include a dredging pause before each spring tide, and admits Mara was right.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Reconcile the guild's firing season with the lock oath.","conflict":"Pell struggles with admitting the trade-off he once refused, and guild families worry about the shortened season.","outcome":"The guild adopts a calendar with a built-in dredging pause, and Pell and Mara reach a wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_silt_to_terraces"]},{"id":"scn_lamps_relit","title":"Lamps on the Lagoon","summary":"At dusk Mara stands at the Glassgate Locks as the tide-mills turn and the lamp vats glow across the lagoon. Sana and Pell's crews share the watch, and Mara records the day's soundings with allies at her side.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mark the restored tide and secure the gates under a shared watch.","conflict":"Mara must let others share the watch rather than holding the gate alone.","outcome":"A shared watch is established and the city's tide-powered lights return, ending the story in hope.","depends_on":["scn_new_calendar"]}]}]}
