aces","summary":"Sana's barge hauls the fertile silt to the Mangrove Terraces, where families spread it as the silt-debt rule demands, and Sana's cooperative earns the dredging contract with its rights recognised.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_sana_duro","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Honour the silt-debt rule and settle the cooperative's contract.","conflict":"Cooperative and terrace families still disagree about shares, and Sana must listen rather than bargain.","outcome":"A fair arrangement is reached on silt shares, and the cooperative's contract is secured.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_the_gates"]},{"id":"scn_new_calendar","title":"A New Calendar","summary":"Pell publicly amends the firing calendar to include a dredging pause before each spring tide, and admits Mara was right.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Reconcile the guild's firing season with the lock oath.","conflict":"Pell struggles with admitting the trade-off he once refused, and guild families worry about the shortened season.","outcome":"The guild adopts a calendar with a built-in dredging pause, and Pell and Mara reach a wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_silt_to_terraces"]},{"id":"scn_lamps_relit","title":"Lamps on the Lagoon","summary":"At dusk Mara stands at the Glassgate Locks as the tide-mills turn and the lamp vats glow across the lagoon. Sana and Pell's crews share the watch, and Mara records the day's soundings with allies at her side.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mark the restored tide and secure the gates under a shared watch.","conflict":"Mara must let others share the watch rather than holding the gate alone.","outcome":"A shared watch is established and the city's tide-powered lights return, ending the story in hope.","depends_on":["scn_new_calendar"]}]}]}
