{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","title":"The Glass Tide","logline":"When junior tide-warden Mara Ilek finds the Glassgate Locks silting shut weeks ahead of schedule, she must win over a proud guild master and a wary barge cooperative to halt the firing season and dredge the gates before the spring tide, or the city loses the tide that powers it.","theme":"Proof persuades only when it is shared and carried together.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Early Silt","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_sounding_poles","title":"The Sounding Poles","summary":"Mara reads the settle lines on her sounding poles at the Glassgate Locks and sees the sills filling weeks faster than the survey predicts. She checks the readings twice in her mother's hand-writing style notes.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm that the locks are silting early.","conflict":"The readings are so far off the tide tables that Mara fears being branded an alarmist like her mother.","outcome":"Mara confirms the early silting and resolves to demand dredging before the spring tide, bound by the lock oath."},{"id":"scn_apprentice_work","title":"Apprentice Work","summary":"Mara carries her notes to Bellmaker's Quay and asks Oren Pell to shorten the firing season. Pell dismisses the soundings as apprentice work and cites the guild calendar.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Persuade Pell to halt the firing season so the gates can be shut and dredged.","conflict":"Mara assumes her numbers will speak for themselves and presents them without allies, while Pell cannot afford the closure and refuses to concede.","outcome":"Pell rejects her request publicly, though privately he knows the tide tables say the same. Mara realizes she needs a way to dredge without the guild's blessing.","depends_on":["scn_sounding_poles"]},{"id":"scn_hiring_the_barge","title":"A Price for the Barge","summary":"Mara goes to the Algae Fields and hires Sana Duro's barge to sound the gate channels. Sana names her price: a say in who owns the dredged silt.","location_id":"loc_algae_fields","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Secure a barge and pilot to sound the channels and later haul dredged silt.","conflict":"Sana bargains hard over silt rights, and Mara cannot promise what the wardens' charter says belongs to the terrace commons.","outcome":"They agree on soundings now and talks on silt later, forming an uneasy alliance.","depends_on":["scn_apprentice_work"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Rising Silt","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_channel_soundings","title":"Soundings in the Fog","summary":"Mara and Sana sound the gate channels at dawn. Sana feels the channel depth through her tiller and Mara reads the settle lines, and together their results show the silting is worse than Mara first measured.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Gather channel-wide evidence of the silting.","conflict":"Fog and shifting sills make readings uncertain, and Sana's mercurial temper clashes with Mara's insistence on precision.","outcome":"They obtain two independent sets of readings showing the gates will choke well before the spring tide.","depends_on":["scn_hiring_the_barge"]},{"id":"scn_silt_rights_dispute","title":"Whose Silt","summary":"On the Mangrove Terraces the wardens and the terrace families argue with Sana about dredged silt. Mara, pressed to promise silt to the commons, hesitates, and Sana bargains when she should listen.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Settle who owns the dredged silt so the dredging contract can proceed.","conflict":"The Ferry Cooperative claims the silt it hauls while the wardens say it belongs to the terrace commons; Sana's bargaining and Mara's rigidity stall talks.","outcome":"Mara accepts that the silt must be spread on the terraces within a season under the silt-debt rule, and Sana agrees to haul it. The terrace families agree to lend hands for dredging.","depends_on":["scn_channel_soundings"]},{"id":"scn_pell_tightens","title":"The Calendar Tightens","summary":"Pell learns of the soundings and the barge. To protect the firing season he pressures the Ferry Cooperative to withhold Sana's barge and keep quiet about the silting.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Keep the locks open through the full firing season by isolating Mara.","conflict":"Pell cannot admit the trade-off he has made, while Sana distrusts the wardens' charter but resents being silenced.","outcome":"Sana refuses to be bought off and leaves with her silence unsold, and Pell tightens the guild's grip on the calendar.","depends_on":["scn_silt_rights_dispute"]},{"id":"scn_guild_hall_failure","title":"Numbers Alone","summary":"Mara brings the combined soundings to the guild hall and recites them. Without allies beside her she is talked over, and Pell's guild masters vote to keep firing.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Win a vote of the guild masters to halt the firing season.","conflict":"Mara's flaw is exposed: the soundings do not persuade by themselves, and her fear of seeming an alarmist makes her hold back her strongest evidence.","outcome":"The guild votes to continue firing and Mara leaves shaken, understanding she must bring witnesses and the terrace families, not just numbers.","depends_on":["scn_pell_tightens"]},{"id":"scn_silted_sill","title":"The Sill Chokes","summary":"A wave of silt stalls the glass gates halfway, and the tide-mills slow, dimming the lamps on the quay. The failure is visible across the lagoon.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Free the stalled gate before the next flood fails to enter the lagoon.","conflict":"The lock oath demands clearing before the spring tide, but the guild still holds the calendar and Pell arrives to see the failure himself.","outcome":"Pell sees the sills for himself and cannot deny what his own tide tables said, while Mara and Sana's evidence is now visible to all.","depends_on":["scn_guild_hall_failure"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spring Tide","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_speaks","title":"Mara Carries the Proof","summary":"Mara returns to the guild hall with Sana, terrace families and the sounding poles, and lets witnesses speak beside her, claiming her mother's name rather than fearing it.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Convince the guild to halt the firing season and release hands for dredging.","conflict":"Pell, unable to admit his earlier trade-off, resists while his guild's families fear lost wages.","outcome":"Pell concedes the season must pause, choosing the lagoon over the calendar, and offers the guild's hands.","depends_on":["scn_silted_sill"]},{"id":"scn_dredge_the_gates","title":"Dredging the Gates","summary":"Guild artisans, terrace families, wardens and Sana's barge dredge the gate channels through the night as the spring tide approaches, Mara reading the settle lines as the work proceeds.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Clear the sills before the spring tide arrives.","conflict":"Time is short, and Pell and Sana must work side by side while Mara must trust others to hold the gate rather than carrying everything herself.","outcome":"The gates are cleared just as the spring tide arrives, and the flood enters the lagoon and restores the tide-mills.","depends_on":["scn_mara_speaks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Tide Returns","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_to_terraces","title":"Silt to the Terraces","summary":"Sana's barge hauls the fertile silt to the Mangrove Terraces, where families spread it as the silt-debt rule demands, and Sana's cooperative earns the dredging contract with its rights recognised.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_sana_duro","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Honour the silt-debt rule and settle the cooperative's contract.","conflict":"Cooperative and terrace families still disagree about shares, and Sana must listen rather than bargain.","outcome":"A fair arrangement is reached on silt shares, and the cooperative's contract is secured.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_the_gates"]},{"id":"scn_new_calendar","title":"A New Calendar","summary":"Pell publicly amends the firing calendar to include a dredging pause before each spring tide, and admits Mara was right.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Reconcile the guild's firing season with the lock oath.","conflict":"Pell struggles with admitting the trade-off he once refused, and guild families worry about the shortened season.","outcome":"The guild adopts a calendar with a built-in dredging pause, and Pell and Mara reach a wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_silt_to_terraces"]},{"id":"scn_lamps_relit","title":"Lamps on the Lagoon","summary":"At dusk Mara stands at the Glassgate Locks as the tide-mills turn and the lamp vats glow across the lagoon. Sana and Pell's crews share the watch, and Mara records the day's soundings with allies at her side.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mark the restored tide and secure the gates under a shared watch.","conflict":"Mara must let others share the watch rather than holding the gate alone.","outcome":"A shared watch is established and the city's tide-powered lights return, ending the story in hope.","depends_on":["scn_new_calendar"]}]}]}
