ees that the second key can only be won by showing Hemo and the weigher side that the evidence is real, and that the weighing is hours away.","depends_on":["scn_lamp_archive_oath"]},{"id":"scn_wells_warning","title":"The Wells Run Dark","summary":"Itho goes to the Erasure Wells to see what awaits a soul weighed against a miscast ledger. He sees an account dissolved and understands the soul will be erased, not merely misjudged.","location_id":"loc_erasure_wells","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Understand exactly what the miscast will cost the soul, and whether it can be undone afterward.","conflict":"The wells dissolve accounts irreversibly, and Itho's obstinacy pushes him to act alone even though the three-key rule forbids it.","outcome":"He confirms that the dead cannot return and only accounts move, so the correction must come before the weighing. He commits to forcing the three keys together in the Hall of Scales.","depends_on":["scn_ors_threatens_hemo"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_chooses","title":"The Lamp and the Page","summary":"Itho returns to Hemo with what he saw at the wells. Hemo, shaken, realises his oath protects the dead but shelters the fraud, and agrees to produce the matching entry by index alone and to attend the weighing.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the third key committed. Hemo wants to act without reading a sealed page.","conflict":"Hemo's fear of losing his lamp and his habit of procedure fight his conscience, and Itho must ask rather than accuse for once.","outcome":"Hemo agrees to bring the matching entry, cross-referenced by his index, to the Hall of Scales. Itho has an ally and a path to two keys, but still needs the weigher's seal.","depends_on":["scn_wells_warning"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Weighing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_weighing_confrontation","title":"The Weighing Before the Scales","summary":"At the Hall of Scales, as the soul is brought forward, Itho and Hemo present the slip and the indexed archive entry in front of the collegium. Dame Ors tries to proceed with the weighing as written.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the three keys sealed before the soul is weighed. Dame Ors wants to weigh the soul as written. Hemo wants to give the correction its third key.","conflict":"Dame Ors's scale-craft lets her read the balance and she argues the error is small, while Hemo's oath and Itho's blunt manner nearly break the case apart.","outcome":"The evidence shows Dame Ors's own seal beside the error. The collegium pauses the weighing, and Dame Ors is forced to decide whether to seal the correction.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_chooses","scn_barred_from_scales"]},{"id":"scn_ors_turns","title":"The Honest Balance","summary":"Dame Ors, reading the soul's weight to the last dram, knows the column is wrong and chooses the scales' honesty over her own reputation. She seals as the weigher, and Itho seals as scribe, with Hemo as lamplighter.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors","chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Complete the three-key seal so the correction stands before the weighing.","conflict":"Dame Ors must put her seal beside the error she certified and give up the story that her concealment was mercy.","outcome":"All three keys are sealed. The ledger is corrected, the soul is weighed against what it actually did, and no soul returns to the living; only the account has moved.","depends_on":["scn_weighing_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Corrected Count","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_aftermath_scales","title":"The Cost of the Seal","summary":"With the soul weighed and at rest, the collegium reckons with the correction. Dame Ors accepts censure for the miscast harvest, and Hemo learns whether his lamp survives.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_id