{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","title":"The Last Audit","logline":"A junior scribe who spots a mis-tallied soul must win three unwilling seals from scribe, weigher and lamplighter before a proud senior weigher weighs the soul against the wrong ledger and sends it to the Erasure Wells.","theme":"A correction is only ink until unwilling hands agree to seal it.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Dropped Letter","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fault_in_the_column","title":"A Fault in the Column","summary":"At his desk in the Counting Halls, Itho Pel copies a mortal account and his fault-sight catches a soul tallied to the wrong ledger column. The soul is already queued for weighing.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Confirm that the entry is truly miscast and not a copying slip of his own.","conflict":"His seniors in the Order of Scribes have waved through similar errors this count, and he trusts ink more than the people who might vouch for it.","outcome":"Itho confirms the miscast, learns the weighing is imminent, and resolves to carry the correction up despite what it will cost him."},{"id":"scn_gate_of_receipts","title":"The Tally-Slip","summary":"Itho goes to the Gate of Receipts to check the soul's tally-slip against the ledger entry. He finds the slip matches the true account, not the column it was entered under.","location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Obtain proof from the soul's own slip that the ledger entry is wrong.","conflict":"Gate clerks will not release a slip from the queue, and the soul is moving toward the Hall of Scales.","outcome":"Itho copies the slip's figures as evidence and learns the weighing is set for the coming bell. He needs a scribe's key first, and the correction will need a weigher's and a lamplighter's after that."},{"id":"scn_senior_scribe_refuses","title":"The Offices That Feed Him","summary":"Itho brings his evidence to the senior scribes, who must vouch for the entry. They refuse to admit a miscast from their own desk, and he says bluntly that they trust the ledger over the truth.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Win the scribe's key, the first of three seals, from his own order.","conflict":"Accusing the offices that feed him risks his post, and his habit of saying so aloud turns the senior scribes against him.","outcome":"He is denied the seal and warned off. He decides to go over their heads to the Collegium of Weighers, and the order he is defying gives him a grudging, conditional scribe's vouch to keep him from escalating further.","depends_on":["scn_fault_in_the_column","scn_gate_of_receipts"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Three Unwilling Hands","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_barred_from_scales","title":"Barred from the Scales","summary":"Itho presents himself at the Hall of Scales and demands a weigher's seal. Dame Ors, who certified the harvest of tallies, receives him with august courtesy and bars a junior scribe from the scales.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Itho wants a weigher's warrant and key. Dame Ors wants the audit quashed and the soul weighed as written.","conflict":"The collegium's rules bar a junior scribe from the scales, and Dame Ors, who knows the column is wrong, calls her concealment mercy and calls the error small.","outcome":"Dame Ors refuses and orders the soul weighed as written. Itho leaves knowing she will not seal the correction, and that she knows the entry is wrong.","depends_on":["scn_senior_scribe_refuses"]},{"id":"scn_counting_halls_pressure","title":"The Desk Is Cleared","summary":"Back in the Counting Halls, Itho finds his desk reassigned on Dame Ors's word. He still holds the copied slip and his notes, and he learns that only the Lamp Archive holds a matching entry that could prove the miscast without his word alone.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Find a proof that does not rest on his say-so.","conflict":"He has lost standing, and his tendency to trust ink over people leaves him without allies among the scribes.","outcome":"Itho resolves to seek the lamplighters, whose archive can answer where his own testimony cannot.","depends_on":["scn_barred_from_scales"]},{"id":"scn_lamp_archive_oath","title":"The Index He May Not Read","summary":"In the Lamp Archive, Itho asks Hemo Lux for the matching entry. Hemo's index memory can locate it without opening the sealed page, but the lamp oath forbids him from reading it aloud and the lamplighters will open no sealed ledger without a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the matching archive entry. Hemo wants to keep the archive honest without breaking his oath.","conflict":"Hemo hides behind procedure, and the sealed-ledger standoff with the weighers means he needs a warrant he cannot get.","outcome":"Hemo will not read the page but admits his index can point to where the proof lies, and says he cannot act without cover. Itho leaves with the position of the matching ledger and Hemo's reluctant interest.","depends_on":["scn_counting_halls_pressure"]},{"id":"scn_ors_threatens_hemo","title":"A Threat to the Lamp","summary":"Dame Ors learns Itho has been to the archive and visits the Lamp Archive herself. She threatens Hemo's lamp if he assists the audit, and Itho, arriving, hears it.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux","chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Dame Ors wants to quash the audit by frightening the archivist. Hemo wants to protect his lamp. Itho wants Hemo's help.","conflict":"The lamp oath makes Hemo vulnerable, and Dame Ors uses it, while Itho's blunt accusation in front of both makes Hemo retreat further into procedure.","outcome":"Hemo declines to commit and Dame Ors leaves satisfied. Itho sees that the second key can only be won by showing Hemo and the weigher side that the evidence is real, and that the weighing is hours away.","depends_on":["scn_lamp_archive_oath"]},{"id":"scn_wells_warning","title":"The Wells Run Dark","summary":"Itho goes to the Erasure Wells to see what awaits a soul weighed against a miscast ledger. He sees an account dissolved and understands the soul will be erased, not merely misjudged.","location_id":"loc_erasure_wells","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Understand exactly what the miscast will cost the soul, and whether it can be undone afterward.","conflict":"The wells dissolve accounts irreversibly, and Itho's obstinacy pushes him to act alone even though the three-key rule forbids it.","outcome":"He confirms that the dead cannot return and only accounts move, so the correction must come before the weighing. He commits to forcing the three keys together in the Hall of Scales.","depends_on":["scn_ors_threatens_hemo"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_chooses","title":"The Lamp and the Page","summary":"Itho returns to Hemo with what he saw at the wells. Hemo, shaken, realises his oath protects the dead but shelters the fraud, and agrees to produce the matching entry by index alone and to attend the weighing.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the third key committed. Hemo wants to act without reading a sealed page.","conflict":"Hemo's fear of losing his lamp and his habit of procedure fight his conscience, and Itho must ask rather than accuse for once.","outcome":"Hemo agrees to bring the matching entry, cross-referenced by his index, to the Hall of Scales. Itho has an ally and a path to two keys, but still needs the weigher's seal.","depends_on":["scn_wells_warning"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Weighing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_weighing_confrontation","title":"The Weighing Before the Scales","summary":"At the Hall of Scales, as the soul is brought forward, Itho and Hemo present the slip and the indexed archive entry in front of the collegium. Dame Ors tries to proceed with the weighing as written.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the three keys sealed before the soul is weighed. Dame Ors wants to weigh the soul as written. Hemo wants to give the correction its third key.","conflict":"Dame Ors's scale-craft lets her read the balance and she argues the error is small, while Hemo's oath and Itho's blunt manner nearly break the case apart.","outcome":"The evidence shows Dame Ors's own seal beside the error. The collegium pauses the weighing, and Dame Ors is forced to decide whether to seal the correction.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_chooses","scn_barred_from_scales"]},{"id":"scn_ors_turns","title":"The Honest Balance","summary":"Dame Ors, reading the soul's weight to the last dram, knows the column is wrong and chooses the scales' honesty over her own reputation. She seals as the weigher, and Itho seals as scribe, with Hemo as lamplighter.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors","chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Complete the three-key seal so the correction stands before the weighing.","conflict":"Dame Ors must put her seal beside the error she certified and give up the story that her concealment was mercy.","outcome":"All three keys are sealed. The ledger is corrected, the soul is weighed against what it actually did, and no soul returns to the living; only the account has moved.","depends_on":["scn_weighing_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Corrected Count","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_aftermath_scales","title":"The Cost of the Seal","summary":"With the soul weighed and at rest, the collegium reckons with the correction. Dame Ors accepts censure for the miscast harvest, and Hemo learns whether his lamp survives.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux","chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Settle the consequences of the correction for the weigher and the lamplighter.","conflict":"The collegium wants to protect its infallibility, while the lamp oath still binds Hemo, who never read the sealed page aloud.","outcome":"Dame Ors admits the error publicly and is censured. Hemo keeps his lamp because he only indexed the page, and the miscast harvest is opened to audit.","depends_on":["scn_ors_turns"]},{"id":"scn_audit_opens","title":"The Audit Begins","summary":"In the Counting Halls, the Order of Scribes is ordered to audit the miscast tallies. Itho is given a desk with a key to the audit rather than a copyist's post, and the scribes who refused him must now work beside him.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Turn one correction into a standing audit of the miscast harvest.","conflict":"The senior scribes resent being corrected by a junior, and Itho must learn to work with the people he distrusted.","outcome":"The audit opens. Itho accepts that a correction depends on others agreeing to seal it, and begins the work with the scribes beside him.","depends_on":["scn_aftermath_scales"]},{"id":"scn_lamp_archive_close","title":"Lamplight on the Index","summary":"Itho visits the Lamp Archive to thank Hemo and file the sealed correction beside the original entry. The two reflect, wry and solemn, that only the accounts moved.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"File the corrected entry in the archive so the record stands.","conflict":"Hemo must decide whether to keep hiding behind procedure now that he has acted, and Itho must decide whether to trust a person as well as ink.","outcome":"The correction is filed and the audit gains an open path through the archive. Itho and Hemo part as allies, with the ledgers a little more honest than before.","depends_on":["scn_audit_opens"]}]}]}
