y. He speaks warmly of his cargo that cannot wait a second turn and hints that the court has always been generous to the season's makers.","location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Qadir wants to learn how far Deva's audit has gone while keeping the first slot he bought.","conflict":"Deva needs his cargo records but he treats every record as something with a price, and his gifts could implicate her if she accepts them.","outcome":"Deva refuses his gifts, and Qadir recognises the audit as a real threat and resolves to contain it.","depends_on":["scn_ink_in_the_grain"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Audit Narrows","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_envoys_argue","title":"The Envoys Argue","summary":"At the Envoy House the three delegations argue their claims under one roof. Deva questions them about the hour they filed and learns each swears the same hour, but only one cannot name the clerk who accepted him.","location_id":"loc_envoy_house","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants testimony that separates the true filing hour from the pre-dated one.","conflict":"The envoys all want the audit to end inconclusive, and they close ranks against a junior scribe.","outcome":"She narrows the suspect entry to the claim tied to Qadir's cargo, though she has no proof.","depends_on":["scn_factor_in_the_rows"]},{"id":"scn_unregistered_gifts","title":"The Unregistered Gifts","summary":"Deva finds goods in the Pepper Warehouses that match no entry in the gift register, delivered to the slot-keepers. Qadir arrives and offers to enter them retroactively, which would clear the keepers and bury her audit.","location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants to prove the slot-keepers were bought, since the gift register rule makes any unentered gift a bribe.","conflict":"Proving it means accusing the office that raised her, and Qadir's offer lets her end the matter safely.","outcome":"Deva refuses, which exposes her to the court, and the slot-keepers move to have her audit halted.","depends_on":["scn_envoys_argue"]},{"id":"scn_audit_halted","title":"The Audit Halted","summary":"In the Harbour Office the senior slot-keepers order Deva to surrender the ledger and close the audit. Her trust in the ledger breaks when she sees a page altered after she copied it, and she realises she must rely on a record the clerks cannot touch.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants to keep the ledger and the audit open until the wind is declared.","conflict":"The office that raised her turns on her and she must accept that the ledger can be forged.","outcome":"She keeps her own memory of every copied entry and decides to take the question to the pilot ghat, where the sea keeps its own record.","depends_on":["scn_unregistered_gifts"]},{"id":"scn_the_pilots_steps","title":"The Pilot's Steps","summary":"On the Pilot Ghat Deva asks Amara, the senior pilot, when the wind first showed signs of turning. Amara explains that she reads the turn a day before the sea shows it, and that her declaration must be given in rite on the true hour.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants Amara's sea-reading to fix the earliest hour a filing could honestly have been made, and Amara wants to declare the wind honestly.","conflict":"Amara speaks in omen-rite the court must take on faith, and every claimant wants her declaration delayed until after their filing stands.","outcome":"Amara agrees to declare on the honest hour, and her timing proves that Qadir's entry was dated before a filing was possible.","depends_on":["scn_audit_halted"]},{"id":"scn_qadirs_price","title":"Qadir's Price","summary":"Qadir, cornered, meets Deva at the Envoy House and offers her office, safety and gifts entered openly in the register if she lets the audit end inconclusive. He also warns that the court will name her the forger.","location_id":"loc_envoy_house","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Qadir wants to keep the first slot until the monsoon is declared.","conflict":"His forged filing saved his season and may cost his name, and Deva must weigh an offer that would protect her but break her purpose.","outcome":"Deva refuses, and Qadir tells the court that she has forged the ledger herself, setting up a public hearing.","depends_on":["scn_the_pilots_steps"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Hour of the Turn","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hearing_at_the_ghat","title":"The Hearing at the Ghat","summary":"At the Pilot Ghat the court gathers for the declaration. Deva names the false entry, Qadir swears over pepper that his filing was first, and Amara declares the turn on the honest hour, which falls after the time Qadir's entry claims.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants to prove the true filing order before the court, and Qadir wants to keep his bought slot.","conflict":"Qadir's oath is binding under the oath-over-pepper rule, and Amara's rite asks the court to take her word on faith.","outcome":"Amara's honest hour proves the pre-dating, Qadir's oath is broken, and the court must follow the true order.","depends_on":["scn_qadirs_price"]},{"id":"scn_qadirs_choice","title":"The Name or the Slot","summary":"Facing ruin, Qadir has one last choice at the ghat: hold to his false claim and lose his name, or confess and surrender the slot. Deva, who has the proof, must decide whether to accuse the whole office or only the man.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Qadir wants to save what he can of his fortune and name, and Deva wants the first slot to go only to whoever filed first.","conflict":"Qadir's belief that every record has a price pulls against a confession, and Deva's loyalty to the office that raised her pulls against naming its keepers.","outcome":"Qadir confesses the pre-dating and the gifts, and Deva enters the full account against the slot-keepers.","depends_on":["scn_hearing_at_the_ghat"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Ledger Re-Entered","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_slot_awarded","title":"The Slot Awarded","summary":"At the Harbour Office the court strikes the forged entry and awards the first sailing slot to the claim filed earliest, as the slot-order rule requires. The envoy who filed truly sails first, and Qadir's cargo waits for the second turn.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants the true filing order entered in the ledger.","conflict":"The slot-keepers resist because their gifts are now exposed, and the court fears the cost of admitting a forged ledger.","outcome":"The ledger is corrected, the keepers are censured for the unregistered gifts, and the slot goes to the honest claimant.","depends_on":["scn_qadirs_choice"]},{"id":"scn_the_fleet_sails","title":"The Fleet Sails","summary":"At the Pepper Warehouses Qadir watches the first fleet load and leave without him, his season cost but his name left standing by his confession. Deva comes to tell him the audit is closed and the court will hear his debts.","location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Qadir wants to salvage his name and credit after losing the slot.","conflict":"His creditors will no longer wait smiling, and Deva must face what the audit cost the man who tempted her.","outcome":"Qadir accepts the loss and begins to rebuild on honest terms, and Deva sees that a record is only as honest as those who write it.","depends_on":["scn_the_slot_awarded"]},{"id":"scn_a_new_hand","title":"A New Hand in the Ledger","summary":"In the Harbour Office Deva sits at the corrected ledger as the court sets new rules for who may write in it. She now signs each entry herself and checks it against the sea's record, which Amara keeps at the ghat.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants to see that the ledger stays honest from here on.","conflict":"Some of the court still resent a junior scribe who accused the office that raised her.","outcome":"Deva is given charge of the filing hours, and the ledger is kept by a hand the court has seen tested.","depends_on":["scn_the_fleet_sails"]}]}]}
